==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=overflow|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|over|flow|lang=en}}.

Literally corresponds to {{term|superfluous|lang=en}}, which is from Latin, rather than Germanic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}}
** {{sense|noun}} {{enPR|ōʹvə-flō'}}, {{IPA|/ˈəʊvəˌfləʊ/|lang=en}}
** {{sense|verb}} {{enPR|ō'və-flōʹ}}, {{IPA|/ˌəʊvəˈfləʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GenAm}}
** {{sense|noun}} {{enPR|ōʹvər-flō'}}, {{IPA|/ˈoʊvɚˌfloʊ/|lang=en}}
** {{sense|verb}} {{enPR|ō'vər-flōʹ}}, {{IPA|/ˌoʊvɚˈfloʊ/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|əʊ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[spillage]] resultant from overflow; [[excess]].
# [[outlet|Outlet]] for escape of excess material.
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} The situation where a value exceeds the available [[numeric]] [[range]].

