===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[flow]] over the [[brim]] of (a [[container]]).
#: ''The river '''overflowed''' the levee.''
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To cover with a liquid, literally or figuratively.
#: ''The flash flood '''overflowed''' most of the parkland and some homes.''
#* '''1851''', Herman Melville, ''Moby-Dick''
#*: So when they were working that evening at the pumps, there was on this head no small gamesomeness slily going on among them, as they stood with their feet continually '''overflowed''' by the rippling clear water {{...}}
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To cause an overflow. {{rfex}}
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To flow over the edge of a container.
#: ''The waters '''overflowed''' into the Ninth Ward.''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To exceed limits or capacity.
#: ''The hospital ER was '''overflowing''' with flu cases.''
## {{context|computing|ambitransitive|lang=en}} To (cause to) [[exceed]] the available [[numeric]] [[range]].
##: ''Calculating 255+1 will '''overflow''' an eight-bit byte.''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To be superabundant; to abound.
#: {{rfquotek|Rogers}}

